  "header": {
    "subsystemType": "Hrot.Scenario",
    "schemaVersion": "1.0",
    "terrainName": "test-town",
    "description": "What: a swarm raid (CE-4621 IM-5; docs/designs/vehicle-tactics/DESIGN_Motorcycle.md \u00a75 / \u00a79). 'Raid Leader' commands six two-up motorcycles ('Bike 1'..'Bike 6', each a 'Rider n' and a 'Pillion n') assembled at the west edge of test-town. SwarmRaid sends each bike to its OWN approach point on a 120 m ring round the post at the road junction (200, 200) (bearings 60\u00b0 apart), then all converge to 20 m of the post, hold 30 s and fight the two 'Post Guard's (Friend, return fire only), ride OUT on divergent bearings (180 m out) and on to the rally point (40, 360). Each phase waits for every live bike (or 180 s). Judge: (1) a bike reaches each of the six approach points (2) all live bikes close to within 30 m of the post together (3) the pillions fire at the post (4) the bikes ride out on divergent bearings (a bike reaches the east and the west out-points) (5) at least four bikes reach the rally point. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh ua-moto-swarm-raid"
  },
